<section class="page-intro wrap"><p class="eyebrow">PLUGINS / THEMES / EXTENSIONS</p><h1>Build something<br><span>of your own.</span></h1><p>Create a plugin or share a theme. The SDK, examples and file formats live alongside the code on GitHub.</p></section><section class="wrap docs-layout"><nav class="docs-nav" aria-label="Developers. topics"><a href="#plugins">Plugin SDK</a><a href="#themes">Theme development</a></nav><div class="status-content"><article id="plugins"><p class="eyebrow">01 / PLUGIN SDK</p><h2>A small API. Useful extensions.</h2><p>The SDK is part of the GitHub source tree. It includes the C API, its implementation, HelloWorld and ARexx examples, build rules and a package validator.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/retrocs-org/beam68/blob/main/sdk/README.md">Plugin SDK documentation ↗</a> · <a href="https://github.com/retrocs-org/beam68/blob/main/sdk/Beam68PluginSDK.guide">AmigaGuide manual ↗</a> · <a href="https://github.com/retrocs-org/beam68/tree/main/sdk/Example">Example plugins ↗</a></p><ul><li>Protocol 1 is the first public protocol. All bundled native plugins return up to eight selectable text, path or query rows in one message.</li><li>Use the SDK to validate hex input and deliver replies to the launcher. ARexx scripts use the documented atomic text transport. Keep previews quick and free of side effects.</li><li>Ship one drawer with an executable and one manifest, including a stable ID, version, trigger and drawer-relative command.</li><li>Run the SDK packaging tool to validate the package. Users install it through Preferences → Plugins.</li></ul><p>Plugins run as native code. Capability labels describe behavior; they do not restrict access. Document dependencies and test on supported AmigaOS systems.</p></article>
<article id="themes"><p class="eyebrow">02 / THEME DEVELOPMENT</p><h2>Five colors. Your atmosphere.</h2><p>Themes use a portable text format rather than a compiled SDK. Start with a bundled file or export a theme from Preferences, edit its colors and import it again.</p><pre><code>#NAME=My Theme
#AUTHOR=Your Name
BEAM68THEME=1
COLORS=FFB000,6B4A00,FFB000,1A1200,140E00</code></pre><p>Each color is a six-digit RGB value. The order is text, shadow, selection fill, selection text and background. Comment metadata can describe the author, name and version. Keep foregrounds readable against both backgrounds.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/retrocs-org/beam68/tree/main/themes">Bundled theme examples ↗</a> · <a href="https://github.com/retrocs-org/beam68/blob/main/src/theme_file.c">Theme file reader and writer ↗</a></p></article>
